(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #115 - the function-return landing site: a function
 declared to `Return a value` hands the caller a runtime-tagged result in
 r11, and reading that call straight into a `text` used to SIGSEGV the
 same way a dynamic map value did before #114. The general fix casts it
 exactly as `'give' of 7 as a text` would.)

To 'give' with a number x.
    Return a value, x.

a text called t is 'give' of 7.
Print "{t}".
